NanOS 2.3.0 model corrections, measured against Cortex Cloud (the official app) on NanOS 2.3.0, 2026-11-17, on the
owner's pedal: sweep presets with a different knob travel on every wire index, each control read in the app (the
numbers are in docs/HANDOFF-NANOS-2.3.md, "Model corrections to make"). Applies on top of 0001.
- Hall, Room, Cave, Modulated, Ambience: Mix is the last wire index; the UI keeps Mix first (wireIndex).
- Upstream's skew wins over #31's fitted curve wherever both exist; #31's curve stays where there is no skew.
- Low-High Cut HPF / LPF 20-20000 Hz (skew 0.3); Graphic 9 LPF 1000-20000 Hz (skew 0.6), HPF 20-20000 Hz (skew 0.3).
- Room Pre Delay 0-100 ms with skew 0.6; Blossom E.R. Length linear.
- Envelope Filter Attack / Decay 10-1000 ms, Level -20..+20 dB, Freq Depth -10000..+10000 Hz, all linear (Freq left).
- Dyn Depth 0-60 dB (skew 0.6); Dual Reverse Delay Trig Threshold -40..0 dB; Circular Delay Feedback 0-95 %,
  High Pass 20-13000 Hz (skew 0.6) and Low Pass 20-20000 Hz (skew 0.61), both fitted on two points (approximate).

